ometres of waymarked walking through the ice age landscape between Kalo and Ebeltoft, normally taken as three stages of about 20 km. It carries the Leading Quality Trail mark.","evidence":{"n_sources":9,"of":12,"urls":["https://eng.nationalparkmolsbjerge.dk/","https://www.traveldiariesapp.com/en/travel-inspiration/denmark/mols-bjerge-national-park","https://www.ebeltoft.dk/en/attractions/mols-bjerge-national-park/"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Kalo castle ruin","type":"activity","detail":"A medieval royal castle on a spit in the bay, reached by a long cobbled causeway across the water.","evidence":{"n_sources":7,"of":12,"urls":["https://eng.nationalparkmolsbjerge.dk/","https://www.traveldiariesapp.com/en/travel-inspiration/denmark/mols-bjerge-national-park","https://evendo.com/locations/denmark/mols-bjerge-national-park/best-attractions"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Trehoje","type":"activity","detail":"Bronze age burial mounds at 127 m, with the whole peninsula below: Aarhus one way, Ebeltoft the other, and the four bays of Kalo, Begtrup, Knebel and Ebeltoft.","evidence":{"n_sources":6,"of":12,"urls":["https://eng.nationalparkmolsbjerge.dk/","https://www.ebeltoft.dk/en/attractions/mols-bjerge-national-park/","https://evendo.com/locations/denmark/mols-bjerge-national-park/best-attractions"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Poskaer Stenhus","type":"activity","detail":"A stone age round dolmen standing in open country, ringed by its own kerb of boulders.","evidence":{"n_sources":6,"of":12,"urls":["https://eng.nationalparkmolsbjerge.dk/","https://www.ebeltoft.dk/en/attractions/mols-bjerge-national-park/","https://evendo.com/locations/denmark/mols-bjerge-national-park/best-attractions"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Ebeltoft old town","type":"activity","detail":"Leaning half timbered houses, cobbles and hollyhocks growing head high against the walls, twenty minutes down the coast.","evidence":{"n_sources":6,"of":12